Click this message to give the app notification permissions";defaultvpn,60,V40198b37f,320198b3ad,;"Default VPN";encrypt_profiles,60,V401fbdfec,3d01fbe025,;"Encrypt profiles";restart,60,V400d0531b,2b00d05342,;"Restart";state_auth_failed,60,V400fb6c0c,4300fb6c4b,;"Authentication failed";restart_vpn_after_change,60,V400d15348,8700d153cb,;"Configuration changes are applied after restarting the VPN. (Re)start the VPN now?";openvpn_log,60,V400de5ef8,3300de5f27,;"OpenVPN Log";session_ipv4string,60,V400ec6877,3a00ec68ad,;"%1$s - %2$s";sorted_az,60,V401a7b926,3d01a7b95f,;"Profiles sorted by name";pw_query_hint,60,V400310dc3,4a00310e09,;"(leave empty to query on demand)";baterry_consumption,60,V400e15fc0,4a200e1645e,;"In my personal tests the main reason for high battery consumption of OpenVPN are the keepalive packets. Most OpenVPN servers have a configuration directive like 'keepalive 10 60' which causes the client and server to exchange keepalive packets every ten seconds. <p> While these packets are small and do not use much traffic\, they keep the mobile radio network busy and increase the energy consumption. (See also <a href=https\://developer.android.com/training/efficient-downloads/efficient-network-access.html#RadioStateMachine>The Radio State Machine | Android Developers</a>) <p> This keepalive setting cannot be changed on the client. Only the system administrator of the OpenVPN can change the setting. <p> Unfortunately using a keepalive larger than 60 seconds with UDP can cause some NAT gateways to drop the connection due to an inactivity timeout. Using TCP with a long keep alive timeout works\, but tunneling TCP over TCP performs extremely poorly on connections with high packet loss. (See <a href=http\://sites.inka.de/bigred/devel/tcp-tcp.html>Why TCP Over TCP Is A Bad Idea</a>)";no_certificate,60,V4001303e0,4800130424,;"You must select a certificate";thanks_for_donation,60,V4012d7ef2,47012d7f35,;"Thanks for donating %s!";no_orbotfound,60,V401d2c69a,8501d2c71b,;"Orbot application cannot be found. Please install Orbot or use manual Socks v5 integration.";faq_system_dialog_xposed,60,V4013b822f,139013b8364,;"If you have rooted your Android device you can install the <a href=\"http\://xposed.info/\">Xposed framework</a> and the <a href=\"http\://repo.xposed.info/module/de.blinkt.vpndialogxposed\">VPN Dialog confirm module</a> at your own risk";add_new_vpn_hint,60,V400d75758,6b00d757bf,;"Use the <img src=\"ic_menu_add\"/> icon to add a new VPN";built_by,60,V401066fe1,3d0106701a,;"built by %1$s (FP\: %2$s)";qs_title,60,V4019cb4d2,2f019cb4fd,;"Toggle VPN";shortcut_profile_notfound,60,V400340e8b,5d00340ee4,;"Profile specified in shortcut not found";tls_key_auth,60,V4004615ed,7e00461667,;"Enables an additional authentication/encryption layer for the OpenVPN control channel";eol_notice_header,1,V4005014e5,3c0050151d,;"End of service";mobile_info,60,V400b544d5,7e00b5454f,;"%10$s %9$s running on %3$s %1$s (%2$s)\, Android %6$s (%7$s) API %4$d\, ABI %5$s\, (%8$s)";using_proxy,60,V400ca511e,3d00ca5157,;"Using proxy %1$s %2$s";searchdomain,60,V4004e1892,35004e18c3,;"searchDomain";broken_images,60,V4009f39f8,37009f3a2b,;"Broken Images";cancel_connection,60,V4003a106e,38003a10a2,;"Disconnect";use_system_proxy,60,V400cb515d,3d00cb5196,;"Use system proxy";official_build,60,V401087055,390108708a,;"official build";allow_translations_summary,60,V401f9defb,b101f9dfa8,;"Allows the app to be translated with translations contributed by the community. Requires a restart of the app to activate.";netstatus,60,V400af425a,3800af428e,;"Network Status\: %s";auth_failed_behaviour,60,V401a9b9ec,4a01a9ba32,;"Behaviour on AUTH_FAILED";protocol,60,V40188ac76,2d0188ac9f,;"Protocol";remove_connection_entry,60,V40177a2f5,4b0177a33c,;"Remove connection entry";clear_log_on_connect,60,V40184aa8e,4c0184aad6,;"Clear log on new connection";ab_not_route_to_vpn_title,60,V40172a13d,580172a191,;"Route to the configured IP address";menu_use_inline_data,60,V4018faeb4,40018faef0,;"Use inline data";dns_server_info,60,V4006720d8,4a0067211e,;"DNS Server\: %1$s\, Domain\: %2$s";faq_shortcut,60,V4007b2a26,3a007b2a5c,;"Shortcut to start";faq_security,60,V4009633fe,3530096374d,;"As OpenVPN is security sensitive a few notes about security are sensible. All data on the sdcard is inherently insecure. Every app can read it (for example this program requires no special sd card rights). The data of this application can only be read by the application itself. By using the import option for cacert/cert/key in the file dialog the data is stored in the VPN profile. The VPN profiles are only accessible by this application. (Do not forget to delete the copies on the sd card afterwards). Even though accessible only by this application the data is still unencrypted. By rooting the telephone or other exploits it may be possible to retrieve the data. Saved passwords are stored in plain text as well. For pkcs12 files it is highly recommended that you import them into the android keystore.";vpn_tethering_title,60,V400e36579,4100e365b6,;"VPN and Tethering";ab_kitkat_reconnect,60,V4016c9e70,134016c9fa0,;"Multiple users report that the mobile connection/mobile data connection is frequently dropped while using the VPN app. The behaviour seems to affect only some mobile provider/device combination and so far no cause/workaround for the bug could be identified. ";data_out,60,V401b1bbb3,2801b1bbd7,;"Out";openvpn3_pkcs12,60,V401cdc4ae,e501cdc58f,;"Using PKCS12 files directly with OpenVPN 3 C\+\+ implementation is not supported. Please import the pkcs12 files into the Android keystore or change to OpenVPN 2.x under general settings.";qs_connect,60,V4019db503,34019db533,;"Connect to %s";message_no_user_edit,60,V4017ea852,90017ea8de,;"This profile has been added from an external app (%s) and has been marked as not user editable.";float_title,60,V4005d1da8,3d005d1de1,;"Allow floating server";use_default_title,60,V400561ae5,3f00561b20,;"Use default Route";custom_config_title,60,V400370f87,4500370fc8,;"Enable Custom Options";useTLSAuth,60,V4001c067a,54001c06ca,;"Use Control Channel Authentication/Encryption";random_host_prefix,60,V400350eea,4100350f27,;"Random Host Prefix";useLZO,60,V4000d026a,32000d0298,;"LZO Compression";settings_auth,60,V400822d77,4300822db6,;"Authentication/Encryption";tls_cipher_alert,60,V4017da4f7,359017da84c,;"Newer OpenVPN for Android versions (0.6.29/March 2015) use a more secure default for the allowed cipher suites (tls-cipher \"DEFAULT\:!EXP\:!PSK\:!SRP\:!kRSA\"). Unfortunately\, omitting the less secure cipher suites and export cipher suites\, especially the omission of cipher suites that do not support Perfect Forward Secrecy (Diffie-Hellman) causes some problems. This usually caused by an well-intentioned but poorly executed attempt to strengthen TLS security by setting tls-cipher on the server or some embedded OSes with stripped down SSL (e.g. MikroTik).
To solve this problem the problem\, set the tls-cipher settings on the server to reasonable default like tls-cipher \"DEFAULT\:!EXP\:!PSK\:!SRP\:!kRSA\". To work around the problem on the client add the custom option tls-cipher DEFAULT on the Android client.";apprest_uuid_desc,1,V400410dd8,d00430e91,;"Unique UUID that identifies the profile (example\: 0E910C15–9A85-4DD9-AE0D-E6862392E638). Generate using uuidgen or similar tools";external_authenticator,60,V401dfcc6a,4901dfccaf,;"External Authenticator";keep,60,V401548d94,2501548db5,;"Keep";cant_read_folder,60,V4000901a0,45000901e1,;"Unable to read directory";channel_description_status,60,V401c3c0c6,7e01c3c140,;"Status changes of the OpenVPN connection (Connecting\, authenticating\,…)";blocklocal_title,60,V4013e8482,4a013e84c8,;"Bypass VPN for local networks";send,60,V40071253f,2500712560,;"Send";ab_only_cidr_title,60,V4016ea047,3e016ea081,;"Non CIDR Routes";pull_off_summary,60,V400491724,7e0049179e,;"No information is requested from the server. Settings need to be specified below.";ignored_pushed_routes,60,V4005319f0,4600531a32,;"Ignore pushed routes";weakmd,60,V401b6bcc3,d01bbbef0,;"<p>Starting with OpenSSL version 1.1\, OpenSSL rejects weak signatures in certificates like MD5. Additionally with the OpenSSL 3.0 signatures with SHA1 are also rejected.</p><p> You should update the VPN certificates as soon as possible as SHA1 will also no longer work on other platforms in the near future.</p> <p>If you really want to use old and broken certificates select insecurefor the TLS security profile under Authentication/Encryption of the profile</p>";editor_close_profile_changed,60,V40208e604,7e0208e67e,;"Profile has changed outside the editor. Closing configuration editor.";timestamps,60,V401338056,3101338083,;"Timestamps";qs_disconnect,60,V4019eb539,37019eb56c,;"Disconnect %s";disallowed_vpn_apps_info,60,V4014e8b7c,4e014e8bc6,;"Disallowed VPN apps\: %1$s";faq_security_title,60,V4009533b6,46009533f8,;"Security considerations";error,60,V400631fe0,2b00632007,;"Error\: ";faq_android_clients,60,V40162910e,5cc016296d6,;"Multiple OpenVPN clients for Android exist. The most common ones are OpenVPN for Android (this client)\, OpenVPN Connect and OpenVPN Settings.<p>The clients can be grouped into two groups\: OpenVPN for Android and OpenVPN Connect use the official VPNService API (Android 4.0\+) and require no root and OpenVPN Settings which uses root.<p>OpenVPN for Android is an open source client and developed by Arne Schwabe. It is targeted at more advanced users and offers many settings and the ability to import profiles from files and to configure/change profiles inside the app. The client is based on the community version of OpenVPN. It is based on the OpenVPN 2.x source code. This client can be seen as the semi officially client of the community. <p>OpenVPN Connect is non open source client that is developed by OpenVPN Technologies\, Inc. The client is indented to be general use client and more targeted at the average user and allows the import of OpenVPN profiles. This client is based on the OpenVPN C\+\+ reimplementation of the OpenVPN protocol (This was required to allow OpenVPN Technologies\, Inc to publish an iOS OpenVPN app). This client is the official client of the OpenVPN technologies <p> OpenVPN Settings is the oldest of the clients and also a UI for the open source OpenVPN. In contrast to OpenVPN for Android it requires root and does not use the VPNService API. It does not depend on Android 4.0\+";route_not_netip,60,V4006d234a,52006d2398,;"Corrected route %1$s/%2$s to %3$s/%2$s";missing_certificates,60,V40192af8f,650192aff0,;"Missing user certificate or user certifcate key file";tls_direction,60,V4001d06d0,4a001d0716,;"Authentication/encryption method";clearappsdialog,60,V401197601,7501197672,;"Clear list of allowed external apps?
